# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Schematic — what does NOT belong in the repository
#
# Rule of thumb: anything generated, machine-specific, or secret is ignored.
# Anything a reader needs in order to trust the project is committed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Dependencies — restored by `npm install`.
# npm workspaces hoist to the root, but a per-workspace node_modules can appear
# too, so this pattern is deliberately unanchored.
node_modules/

# Build output — restored by `npm run build`.
dist/
build/
out/

# Secrets. Keys are typed into the browser and sent per request; the server never
# stores one, so no .env file is needed to run this project at all. These patterns
# exist so a key pasted into a local file can never be committed by accident.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# TypeScript incremental build info — machine-specific, rewritten on every build.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Caches
.vite/
.cache/
.eslintcache
.parcel-cache/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# Test / coverage output
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editors and IDEs
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Scratch files and archives
*.tgz
*.tmp
tmp/
temp/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deliberately NOT ignored: verify/evidence/
#
# That directory holds the raw JSON behind every claim in VERIFICATION.md. It is
# generated output, but it is the audit trail — the entire point of this project is
# that its claims can be re-read rather than taken on trust. Re-running
# `node verify/e2e.mjs` rewrites it, so expect those files to change in a diff.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

docs/